version: 2.0.0
components:
  MemorySection:
    description: >-
      Memory Steward ledger section in the Platform UI (Phase C1 + C2/C3,
      TD-2026-09-20-669). Header band shows scanned/pinned/findings counts off the
      /api/memory/review digest. Two-column body: a Ledger (the advisory hygiene
      digest grouped by suggestion in the CLI's heading order — prune / merge /
      route:habits / route:task / route:decisions / route:lore / pin) beside the
      SyncPreviewPanel. fetchReview on mount. Surfaces the store's single last
      actionError as a dismissible inline banner above the ledger. Rows carry
      one-click apply buttons (C2) and the sync panel carries the gated --write
      apply (C3).
    type: view
    tags: [feature, memory, platform]
  LedgerGroup:
    description: >-
      One suggestion bucket in the ledger. Renders the CLI's SUGGESTION_HEADINGS
      label (reused verbatim so the web ledger reads identically to `paradigm
      memory review`) + a count, then a column of LedgerRows. Self-hides when the
      bucket is empty.
    type: component
    tags: [feature, memory, platform]
  LedgerRow:
    description: >-
      A single memory-entry finding — name, staleness score (0–1, color-ramped),
      graph-validity verdict, rationale, the equivalent applyCommand as a code
      chip, and (C2) a one-click apply button driven by the row's suggestion
      (prune → prune; route:* → route with the matching to; merge → merge the
      whole cluster; pin → pin) via store.applyRow. Prune confirms first (it
      archives a file). While any row action is in flight all buttons disable.
    type: component
    tags: [feature, memory, platform]
  SyncPreviewPanel:
    description: >-
      The lean-rewrite PREVIEW off /api/memory/sync (computeSync is pure — no
      write). Shows bytesBefore→bytesAfter, lines, changed/already-lean status,
      demoted[] leaf entries (heading + reason + applyHint), deduped[] blocks, a
      projection checkbox that refetches with projection=true and lists
      projectionItems[], and the unified diff in a monospace scroll box. (C3) When
      the preview would change MEMORY.md it exposes an explicit "Apply sync
      (--write)" button that confirms, POSTs /api/memory/sync/write with the
      current projection toggle, and on success shows the backupPath + refetches
      the preview. Makes clear it writes MEMORY.md (backed up first).
    type: component
    tags: [feature, memory, platform]
  memoryStore:
    description: >-
      Zustand store for the Memory section (mirrors tasksStore's fetch/abort +
      runAction pattern). Holds the review digest + the sync preview (each with its
      own AbortController + loading/error state) and the projection toggle.
      fetchReview → GET /api/memory/review; fetchSync(projection) → GET
      /api/memory/sync?projection=. (C2/C3) applyRow(item) maps the suggestion →
      the matching write endpoint (prune/route/merge/pin), POSTs, and on success
      re-fetches BOTH review + sync; actionPendingId/actionError drive per-row
      pending + inline error. applySyncWrite() POSTs /api/memory/sync/write and
      holds syncWriting + syncWriteResult{ wrote, backupPath, bytesAfter }.
    type: state
    tags: [feature, memory, platform, state]
